<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mastino II della Scala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1308">1308</a>–<a href="/years/1351">1351</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mastino II della Scala was lord of Verona from 1329, nephew of Cangrande I. He extended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaliger</a> rule to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a>, Parma and Lucca, but a coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> defeated him in 1336–1339, stripping him of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, Treviso and other cities. He kept Verona and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a> until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mastino-ii-della-scala.jpg" alt="Mastino II della Scala" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ugo franchini · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mastino_II_della_Scala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
